# Round 5 for the Fox: a new face set that looks like she does in round 4, made to drop onto the head she now has. Writes the page with copy buttons and the project note.
import html
RULES = "Keep her exactly the woman in the attached paintings: the same face, the same age, the same freckles, the same warm brown eyes, the same soft full cheeks. Do not make her older, thinner or sterner. Painted as realistically as those paintings, on a flat plum background (#3B2F43), with soft even light from the front and no shadow across her face. She is NOT wearing her glasses. No teeth are visible in any picture."
P = [
 ("F1", "Her face, straight on", "Square", "Attach: J9 (Pins and Needles), J11 (Thimble), C3 (three views).",
  "Stay on this one until it is her. Everything else is made from it.",
  "Square image. One very large close-up painting of her face from directly in front, filling the frame from the top of her forehead to just under her chin, with both of her own ears inside the frame. Her curls are tucked back behind her ears so the whole outline of her face is clear, and no hair crosses her forehead, temples or cheeks. Her costume fox ears are not in the picture. Lips closed in a small, warm, closed-lip smile. Eyes open, looking straight at the viewer. Head perfectly level, not tilted and not turned. " + RULES),
 ("F2", "Six states of her face", "Wide, 3:2", "Attach: your finished F1.",
  "This gives her blink, her talking mouths and her smile. Each face must sit in the same place in its box.",
  "Wide image, landscape 3:2. A grid of six close-up paintings of the same face, three across and two down, each exactly the same size, each from directly in front with the head perfectly level, each in exactly the same position inside its box, each showing from her eyebrows' top to just under her chin. Every one matches the attached face exactly except for the one change named. Top row, left to right: (1) the attached face unchanged; (2) both eyes gently closed, as in the middle of a blink, mouth unchanged; (3) both eyes half closed, upper lids lowered halfway over the eyes, mouth unchanged. Bottom row, left to right: (4) lips just parted as if starting to speak, eyes unchanged; (5) lips rounded in a small 'oo', eyes unchanged; (6) a broader, happy closed-lip smile with her cheeks lifted, eyes unchanged. " + RULES),
 ("F3", "Front, turned and side", "Wide, 3:2", "Attach: your finished F1, and C3.",
  "The side view is what shapes her head, so her forehead, nose, lips, chin and jaw must be clear against the background.",
  "Wide image, landscape 3:2. Three large paintings of her head and neck side by side at exactly the same size, each showing from the top of her hair down to her collarbones. Left: from directly in front. Middle: her head turned 45 degrees toward the right edge of the image. Right: an exact side view, a true profile, facing the right edge. Her hair is drawn up into the tall pile of curls on top of her head as in the attached paintings, with the curls at her temples swept back so that her forehead, the bridge and tip of her nose, her lips, her chin, her jawline and her whole ear are clear against the background. Her costume fox ears are not in the picture. Small closed-lip smile, eyes open, head level. " + RULES),
]
WHY = [
 "She now has the Jester's 3D head with <b>her own painted face</b> on it, so she is no longer the Jester. That face comes from sheet C3, where it is small (about 107 pixels between her pupils), so it is soft close up.",
 "These three pictures give her a face as large and sharp as the Jester's, looking the way she does in round 4. They are framed so I can lay them on the head by the eyes and mouth without stretching the rest.",
 "Order: F1 first, until it is her. Then F2 and F3, each with F1 attached. No teeth in any of them.",
]
page = ["<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset='utf-8'><meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width,initial-scale=1'><title>Fox · Round 5 · Face</title><style>body{font:16px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif;background:#2a2233;color:#f1e9f5;margin:0;padding:16px;max-width:760px;margin:auto}h1{font-size:22px}h2{font-size:18px;margin:26px 0 4px;color:#ffd98a}.m{color:#cbbfd6;font-size:14px}.p{background:#1d1724;border:1px solid #54456a;border-radius:10px;padding:12px;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:14.5px}button{background:#ffd98a;color:#2a2233;border:0;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 16px;font-weight:700;font-size:15px;margin:8px 0}li{margin:6px 0}</style></head><body><h1>Fox Witch · Round 5 · her face</h1><ul>"]
page += ["<li>%s</li>" % w for w in WHY]; page.append("</ul>")
for k, t, shape, att, note, pr in P:
    page.append("<h2>%s · %s</h2><div class='m'>%s. %s<br>%s</div><button onclick=\"navigator.clipboard.writeText(document.getElementById('%s').textContent);this.textContent='Copied'\">Copy prompt</button><div class='p' id='%s'>%s</div>" % (k, html.escape(t), shape, html.escape(att), html.escape(note), k, k, html.escape(pr)))
page.append("</body></html>"); open('/home/claude/work/fox_r5/Fox_Round5_Face_Prompts.html', 'w').write(''.join(page))
import re
md = ["# Fox Witch – round 5: a new face set\n\nWritten by Claude, 12 Nov 2026, after Chris said: the Jester's face looks good on her but \"it's still the Jester\"; the four are unique characters; he wants the Fox to look like she does in round 4 and suggested another set of face images.\n\n## Why\n"]
md += ["- " + re.sub(r"</?b>", "**", w) for w in WHY]
md.append("\n## Rules in every prompt\n\n" + RULES + "\n")
for k, t, shape, att, note, pr in P: md.append("## %s: %s (%s)\n\n%s %s\n\n```\n%s\n```\n" % (k, t, shape, att, note, pr))
md.append("## What I do with them\n\n- F1 becomes her face picture, laid on the head by pupils and lip line (the head's own frame: eyes at 1.5246, lip line 0.066 below). Pupils are read off a gridded copy by eye, never found automatically.\n- F2 gives the states: eyes shut, eyes half shut, two talking mouths, a closed smile. Each is cut as a soft-edged patch and set into F1.\n- F3's side view is the check for the head's shape, and gives the paint for cheek and jaw at the sides.\n- No teeth, anywhere (Chris's standing rule).\n")
open('/home/claude/work/fox_r5/fox-3d-round5-face-prompts.md', 'w').write('\n'.join(md)); print('ok')
